    icon: 'Activity',
    concepts: [
      { id: 'mo-1', term: 'Metrics & Time Series', summary: 'Numeric observations over time for systems.', detail: 'Metrics capture countable signals: request count, latency, queue depth, CPU usage. Use Prometheus counters, gauges, histograms, and summaries. Recording rules precompute expensive aggregations and reduce dashboard query load.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-2', term: 'Structured Logging', summary: 'Machine-parseable logs with consistent fields.', detail: 'JSON logs include timestamp, service, severity, correlation IDs, and environment fields. They improve search, aggregation, and incident correlation. Centralize logs and redact secrets before shipping.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-3', term: 'Distributed Tracing', summary: 'Request journeys across microservices and databases.', detail: 'Traces contain spans representing work in each service. Trace IDs correlate spans across services. Use trace sampling rules and span attributes to keep signal without overwhelming storage.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-4', term: 'OpenTelemetry', summary: 'Vendor-neutral instrumentation standard.', detail: 'OTel provides SDKs, auto-instrumentation, and a collector pipeline for metrics, logs, and traces. It reduces backend lock-in and gives portable observability across languages and runtimes.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-5', term: 'SLOs & Error Budgets', summary: 'Reliability targets with measurable tolerance.', detail: 'SLIs measure behavior. SLOs set target levels. Error budgets are the difference between perfect and acceptable. Use burn-rate alerting to detect fast consumption before users notice.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-6', term: 'Alerting Quality', summary: 'Low-noise, actionable alerts with runbooks.', detail: 'Good alerts require human action now. Use severity tiers and routing. Reduce false positives with high thresholds, multi-window checks, and longer evaluation windows after deployments.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-7', term: 'Dashboards & RED Method', summary: 'Focused service health dashboards.', detail: 'Use RED: Rate, Errors, Duration. Show golden signals, dependency latency, and SLO burn. Role-based dashboards prevent overload.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-8', term: 'On-call & Incident Response', summary: 'Reliable structured responses to production issues.', detail: 'Define incident roles, escalation paths, severity levels, and communication templates. Separate detection, mitigation, and postmortem activities. Track MTTA and MTTR metrics and improve runbooks after each incident.', category: 'Cloud' },
      { id: 'mo-9', term: 'Synthetic Monitoring', summary: 'Active probes that test like users.', detail: 'Synthetics validate endpoints, APIs, and transactions from external viewpoints. They catch outages before user reports. Complement with passive telemetry for full coverage.', category: 'Cloud' },
    ],
